Just wanted to resurrect this thread long enough to mention that I too
have finally sworn off on graphics, thanks to two recent supremely
aggravating deaths.

The first was caused by the "feature" in Qt Nethack that clicking the
mouse anywhere on the map will hustle your character to that
location.  These days I generally play on my MacBook, and the ball of
my right thumb often rests perilously near the single wide mouse
button beneath the trackpad.  Occasionally I would see my character
spontaneously trek to a new location, apparently of his own volition.
Very mysterious, until I figured out what was happening.  I couldn't
find a way to turn that feature off, so I just tried to be careful.
My caution failed me, however, when I was chasing Lord Surtur on the
Valkyrie quest and my character committed suicide by suddenly diving
headlong into the lava.

You'd think that would be enough to teach me, but no.  Soon after, I
reached Medusa's Lair in a new game.  I had an amulet of reflection
from Sokoban, but I put on a blindfold for good measure--I don't get
to Medusa very often, and I didn't want to screw it up.  After one
hit, Medusa disappeared from my telepathy.  I was puzzled, and stalked
around the room for a bit, hoping to stumble across her corpse.
Eventually I peeked from under my blindfold; she was gone.  Weird, I
thought; I guess I killed her in one hit and she didn't leave a
corpse.  I swapped out my amulet of reflection for an amulet of life
saving and continued down to the Castle, where I decided that my -5 AC
probably wasn't up to the task of storming it.  I headed back up to
the main dungeon, and who do you think I ran into on the level above
Medusa's?

Medusa, of course.  I tapped H a bunch of times to leave the room with
the downstair, and suddenly I was dead.  Medusa was lurking just
outside the door.  My amulet of life saving saved me once, but because
all of the messages describing what was happened scrolled up so
rapidly, I didn't even notice, and with my next oblivious step after
that, I was petrified.  ARGH.

It's terminal mode for me from now on, all the way.


